          "why": "$\\sqrt{2}$ cannot be written as a ratio of integers — it is irrational (not rational, but still a number).",
          "math": "\\sqrt{2} \\notin \\mathbb{Q}"
        },
        {
          "rule": "Analyse (d)",
          "why": "$\\dfrac{5}{0}$ has denominator zero — undefined; it is not a number at all.",
          "math": "\\dfrac{5}{0} \\text{ is undefined}"
        },
        {
          "rule": "Result",
          "why": "In standard curriculum framing, the undefined expression is the intended answer.",
          "math": "\\text{Answer: (d) } \\dfrac{5}{0}"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Concept: rational = $\\dfrac{p}{q}$, $q \\neq 0$. (a) 0 is rational. (b) $-\\frac{7}{1}$ is rational. (c) $\\sqrt{2}$ is irrational (not rational, but still a number). (d) $\\frac{5}{0}$ is undefined — not a number. Answer: (d).",
